# SafeMining Online Sync

## Offline-first

MVP runs with `IBManager.ConnectionMode.Offline`. All session data must persist locally before any HTTP attempt.

## Local files (persistentDataPath)

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `ScorePersistantData.json` | Existing ScoreManager history |
| `PendingSyncQueue.json` | Outbound sync queue |
| `SimulationSessionContext.json` | Active/completed session context |

## DTO to Enterprise Architect mapping

| Unity DTO | EA Entity |
|---|---|
| `SimulationSessionContext` | `IntentoCapacitacionCapacitado` |
| `SimulationEventRecord` | `EleccionOpcionCapacitacion` |
| `SimulationObjectiveResult` | `OBJETIVOSCapacitacion` / partial result |
| `SimulationResultPayload` | `resultadoIntentoCapacitacion` |

## API contracts (future — Fase 7)

- `POST /api/vr/sessions/start` — create attempt, return intentoId
- `POST /api/vr/sessions/{id}/events` — record interaction
- `POST /api/vr/sessions/{id}/complete` — finalize score and approval
- `POST /api/vr/sessions/sync` — batch deferred entries (24h window per HU-220 CA8)

## Adapter pattern

- `ISimulationBackendAdapter` — abstraction
- `OfflineBackendAdapter` — queue only, no HTTP
- `SafeMiningBackendAdapter` — REST stub until backend ready

## IBManager legacy

Keep `IBManager.SendScoreToCloud` and `/crearSimReporte` intact. New sync layer runs in parallel via `SyncQueueManager`. Do not break offline menu flow.

## ALWAYS

1. Use `JsonUtility` with wrapper classes for lists
2. Purge sync entries older than 24 hours on flush
3. Enqueue on `ScoreManager.EndScene` via `EnqueueCompleteFromSceneScore`

## NEVER

1. Block gameplay when network unavailable
2. Delete local score history on sync failure
3. Send PII beyond participantId/sessionId defined in session context
